  "body": "This is fork from https://github.com/w3c/html/issues/932\r\n\r\nOriginal issue\r\n\r\n> `<optgroup>` is useful for displaying options to users, but browsers don't support it with `<datalist>`.\r\n> \r\n> 4.10.9 The optgroup element has only one context specified for `<optgroup>`\r\n> \r\n>     As a child of a select element.\r\n> \r\n> This issue suggests adding another\r\n> \r\n>     As a child of a datalist element.\r\n> \r\n> or in some other way specifying that browsers should support `<optgroup>` when displaying options on a `<datalist>` 🙏\r\n\r\n",
